                    <div class="layout__header-content">
                        
                        <h1>Focus for PSC: Oily water separator sampling point</h1>
                        
                    </div>
                    <div class="layout__media">
                            <figure class="banner-block__media">
                                <img src="/contentassets/1377ac405b2444ed991e8f26dcc2afd4/transformation-illustration-white-on-dark-blue1134x350.png" alt="Focus for PSC: Oily water separator sampling point"
                                     class="banner-block__media-content" loading="eager" />
                            </figure>
                    </div>
            </header>


    <div class="layout__main">
        <p class="intro"><span>The MEPC.107(49) requires a sampling point to be installed in a vertical section of the outlet pipe as close as possible to the 15 ppm bilge separator outlet. There have been several cases where ships have been detained for not complying with this requirement. This technical news summarizes this topic.</span></p>
            
